[size=12pt][b]Where this node is behind[/b][/size]

[table]
[tr][td][b]module[/b][/td][td][b]Core[/b][/td][td][b]bmc[/b][/td][td][b]ratio[/b][/td][td][b]why[/b][/td][/tr]
[tr][td]MuHash finalize ([tt]MuHashFinalize[/tt]: the [tt]gettxoutsetinfo[/tt] digest)[/td][td]28.0 us[/td][td]1,861 us[/td][td][b]66x slower[/b][/td][td]our 3072-bit inverse is a Fermat exponentiation, 6,142 modular multiplies; Core's is a safegcd. Paid once per RPC call, never per block.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]ElligatorSwift key creation ([tt]EllSwiftCreate[/tt])[/td][td]18.0 us[/td][td]119.8 us[/td][td][b]6.6x slower[/b][/td][td]plain C over the asm field arithmetic; once per BIP324 connection[/td][/tr]
